Relevant columns and why we need them  
• `fullVisitorId` : visitor / customer identifier to tie all the purchases of the same person  
• `hits` (repeated RECORD) : contains every hit that happened in a session  
• `hits.type` : we only want rows where the hit actually represents an ITEM that was bought (`hits.type = 'ITEM'`)  
• `hits.item.productName` : the name of each product that was purchased – used to (a) find purchasers of “Youtube Men’s Vintage Henley” and (b) list the other products they bought  
• `hits.item.itemQuantity` : quantity sold – lets us rank products by units sold  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` (automatic pseudo‑column when wildcarding) : lets us restrict the scan to July‑2017 tables only (`ga_sessions_201707*`)  
• `date` (string) : second way to check the day if desired (all July 2017 = '20170701' … '20170731')  

Typical filter / join conditions that will be used  
• `FROM \`bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*\`` – wildcard over all July‑2017 daily tables  
• `UNNEST(hits)  AS h` – flatten repeated hits records  
• `WHERE h.type = 'ITEM'` – keep only ecommerce ITEM rows  
• `WHERE LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'` – find the “Youtube Men’s Vintage Henley” product (use LOWER + LIKE to dodge typographic apostrophes)  
• `AND s.fullVisitorId IN ( … )` – restrict to customers who bought that item  
• `AND LOWER(h.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%henley%'` – exclude the Henley itself when counting other products  

------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final SQLs (all return ≤ 20 rows)  
```sql
-- 1. Peek at distinct product names sold in July‑2017 (first 20)
SELECT DISTINCT h.item.productName
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. What do product names containing the word “henley” look like?
SELECT DISTINCT h.item.productName
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
  AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%henley%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. List the first 20 visitors that bought any “henley” product
SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
  AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%henley%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Check whether the exact string “youtube men’s vintage henley” exists
SELECT DISTINCT h.item.productName
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
  AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count how many unique customers bought the Henley
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId) AS henley_buyers
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
  AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%';
```

```sql
-- 6. Bring back all purchases made by those Henley buyers (sample 20 rows)
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
)
SELECT s.fullVisitorId,
       h.item.productName,
       h.item.itemQuantity
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
JOIN   henley_buyers hb
  ON   s.fullVisitorId = hb.fullVisitorId
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate quantities per product for Henley buyers (including the Henley)
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
)
SELECT  h.item.productName,
        SUM(h.item.itemQuantity) AS units_sold
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
JOIN   henley_buyers hb
  ON   s.fullVisitorId = hb.fullVisitorId
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
GROUP BY h.item.productName
ORDER BY units_sold DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but EXCLUDING the Henley itself
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
)
SELECT  h.item.productName,
        SUM(h.item.itemQuantity) AS units_sold
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
JOIN   henley_buyers hb
  ON   s.fullVisitorId = hb.fullVisitorId
WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
  AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
GROUP BY h.item.productName
ORDER BY units_sold DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Add tie‑breakers: also rank by #distinct customers
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
),
sales AS (
  SELECT h.item.productName AS product_name,
         h.item.itemQuantity  AS qty,
         s.fullVisitorId      AS buyer
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  JOIN   henley_buyers hb
    ON   s.fullVisitorId = hb.fullVisitorId
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
)
SELECT  product_name,
        SUM(qty)                   AS total_units,
        COUNT(DISTINCT buyer)      AS buying_customers
FROM    sales
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_units DESC, buying_customers DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER – the single top‑selling product (by units) among
--     July‑2017 customers who bought “Youtube Men’s Vintage Henley”, excluding that item
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
),
other_sales AS (
  SELECT h.item.productName  AS product_name,
         h.item.itemQuantity AS qty
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_201707*` AS s,
         UNNEST(s.hits) AS h
  JOIN   henley_buyers hb
    ON   s.fullVisitorId = hb.fullVisitorId
  WHERE  h.type = 'ITEM'
    AND  LOWER(h.item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%henley%'
)
SELECT  product_name,
        SUM(qty) AS total_units_sold
FROM    other_sales
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_units_sold DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
Each query returns up to 20 rows (or 1 row in the last case) so you can quickly inspect intermediary results and ultimately identify the top‑selling product for the requested segment.
